net/packet: fix a race in packet_set_ring() and packet_notifier()

jira KERNEL-1812
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.178.1.el8_10
commit-author Quang Le <quanglex97@gmail.com>
commit 01d3c8417b9c1b884a8a981a3b886da556512f36
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.178.1.el8_10/01d3c841.failed

When packet_set_ring() releases po->bind_lock, another thread can
run packet_notifier() and process an NETDEV_UP event.

This race and the fix are both similar to that of commit 15fe076edea7
("net/packet: fix a race in packet_bind() and packet_notifier()").

There too the packet_notifier NETDEV_UP event managed to run while a
po->bind_lock critical section had to be temporarily released. And
the fix was similarly to temporarily set po->num to zero to keep
the socket unhooked until the lock is retaken.

The po->bind_lock in packet_set_ring and packet_notifier precede the
introduction of git history.

Fixes: 1da177e4c3f4 ("Linux-2.6.12-rc2")
	Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
	Signed-off-by: Quang Le <quanglex97@gmail.com>
	Signed-off-by: Willem de Bruijn <willemb@google.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20250801175423.2970334-1-willemdebruijn.kernel@gmail.com
	Signed-off-by: Jakub Kicinski <kuba@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit 01d3c8417b9c1b884a8a981a3b886da556512f36)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	net/packet/af_packet.c
diff --cc net/packet/af_packet.c
index 5d0ebb2ec763,a7017d7f0927..000000000000
--- a/net/packet/af_packet.c
+++ b/net/packet/af_packet.c
@@@ -4363,12 -4571,12 +4363,17 @@@ static int packet_set_ring(struct sock 
  
  	/* Detach socket from network */
  	spin_lock(&po->bind_lock);
 -	was_running = packet_sock_flag(po, PACKET_SOCK_RUNNING);
 +	was_running = po->running;
  	num = po->num;
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +	if (was_running) {
 +		po->num = 0;
++=======
+ 	WRITE_ONCE(po->num, 0);
+ 	if (was_running)
++>>>>>>> 01d3c8417b9c (net/packet: fix a race in packet_set_ring() and packet_notifier())
  		__unregister_prot_hook(sk, false);
- 	}
+ 
  	spin_unlock(&po->bind_lock);
  
  	synchronize_net();
@@@ -4398,10 -4608,10 +4403,15 @@@
  	mutex_unlock(&po->pg_vec_lock);
  
  	spin_lock(&po->bind_lock);
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +	if (was_running) {
 +		po->num = num;
++=======
+ 	WRITE_ONCE(po->num, num);
+ 	if (was_running)
++>>>>>>> 01d3c8417b9c (net/packet: fix a race in packet_set_ring() and packet_notifier())
  		register_prot_hook(sk);
- 	}
+ 
  	spin_unlock(&po->bind_lock);
  	if (pg_vec && (po->tp_version > TPACKET_V2)) {
  		/* Because we don't support block-based V3 on tx-ring */
* Unmerged path net/packet/af_packet.c
